.Dd August 5, 2026
.Dt NITEMS 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nitems
.Nd number of elements in an array
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.Fn nitems "array"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn nitems
macro expands to the number of elements in
.Fa array .
.Fa nitems
is equivalent to
.Pq sizeof(array) / sizeof((array)[0]) .
.Pp
.Fa array
must be a true array object.
Providing a pointer quantity will result in an incorrect result because
.Li sizeof
for a pointer will compute size of the pointer type, not the size of the memory which the pointer refers to.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
static const int table[] = {1, 2, 3, 4};
for (size_t i = 0; i < nitems(table); i++)
    printf("%d\en", table[i]);
.Ed
